WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:11.417
This is Idea to Edit, a new feature concept for CapCut. Give it one idea, and AI builds the visuals, motion, music and the final cut. And every track stays editable.

2
00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:16.055
Option one: start from text. A sentence or a short story is enough.

3
00:00:16.995 --> 00:00:20.619
Want a specific look or style? Attach a reference image first.

4
00:00:20.974 --> 00:00:26.565
Generate a full draft right away, or refine the storyboard first. Let's look at the storyboard.

5
00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:34.124
AI works step by step: it reads the idea, sets up the characters, picks a style, then breaks it into shots.

6
00:00:34.483 --> 00:00:39.082
Each character gets a reference image, a look profile that every shot follows.

7
00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:47.522
Every cell is editable. Pick the shot size and camera from a list. The shot details are lighting and framing notes added by AI.

8
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.667
Add a line of dialogue anywhere. The avatars show who's in the shot.

9
00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.161
AI even suggests an extra shot. One click to accept.

10
00:00:56.532 --> 00:00:58.984
Happy with it? Generate from this storyboard.

11
00:00:59.411 --> 00:01:04.647
Clips fill the timeline one by one, with music, sound effects and voice on their own tracks.

12
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.126
The first draft is ready, with storyboard, preview and timeline all linked.

13
00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:16.109
The top row holds the emotion nodes: what each part should make the viewer feel.

14
00:01:17.362 --> 00:01:23.582
Change one, and that part's color, pacing and music change together. The characters and story stay the same.

15
00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:29.982
Say we want this part more upbeat, at strong intensity. It first explains what it plans to change.

16
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:37.372
You get candidates first, and apply them only when you like the preview.

17
00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:46.231
Only a few spots feel off? Mark those clips, and describe each problem.

18
00:01:46.585 --> 00:01:49.822
One click redoes them all. Everything else stays untouched.

19
00:01:50.991 --> 00:01:54.033
Compare side by side: clip eight is now a close-up.

20
00:01:54.388 --> 00:01:56.852
Apply when you're happy. You can always undo.

21
00:01:59.145 --> 00:02:02.219
You can also start from a photo, like your dog at home.

22
00:02:03.147 --> 00:02:08.230
AI reads the photo first: the subject, the scene, the mood, and a story worth telling.

23
00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:14.404
Then it offers three directions: bring it to life, make a short film, or create an animated poster.

24
00:02:15.361 --> 00:02:19.254
Bring it to life: the first frame is your photo, and then it starts to move.

25
00:02:27.594 --> 00:02:33.227
One idea, or one photo, becomes a video you can keep editing. That's Idea to Edit.
